Hi,
I'm experimenting some problems with the hda-intel module because my
soundcard isn't recognized by the module (in fact, the module find that
it's a hda-intel but it doesn't know the codec to use and try guessing
by the bios). I've tried to use other codecs but it just ignore it ie:
modprobe snd-hda-intel model=6stck-dig
give me :
hda_codec: Unknown model for ALC882, trying auto-probe from BIOS...

The card is an integrated on an Asus P5WD.
There are 6 jack on the card plus 1 spdif coax, 1 spdif optical and 1
connexion on the motherboard for mic and line out for the case front
(can be used in hda mode or legacy AC97 mode). There is also something
special, a connector for using the speakers the the computer is off.

Right now, the card works, but there are some quirks:
- there is no master control and some apps aren't happy at all about it,
- the digital out is not in a common place (I don't know how to say it
  better. In the apps, it used to be used like this :
  AES0=0x6,AES1=0x82,AES2=0x0,AES3=0x2
  but here, I have to use:
  AES0=0x6,AES1=0x82,AES2=0x0,AES3=0x1
  (it hard to find the meaning of this, I didn't found it in the docs, 
   it was a trial-error guessing, with the help of /proc/asound/devices)
- sometimes, (in fact, never with the 1.0.13 of the drivers but very   
  often with the 1.0.14) the digital out seems to be frozen when 
  sending ac3 by pass trough. I mean,ie I use it for stereo sound, OK,
  I try to watch a DVD, no sound goes out and my speaker system tries
  to detect the kind of thing I'm sending to them, I quit the DVD app,
  I try to listen to music and, there is no more sound on this channel
  (the speakers always try to detect the kind of data, I have tried to
   shut them off and on, but it's always the same). Maybe it's another,
   problem and, when the 1.0.14 will be released, I'll report it if it 
   persist.

The more annoying thing is the lack of master control.

Do you think I can provide you enough informations to correct it or
you need some specs from Asus ?

Nicolas.

PS: I'm not a c programmer (nor c++) so I just can help you giving
informations or trying some procedures for you (I regret that, trust me)
If you need more informations, just ask me.

Sorry for the size of this mail.

